Test Cases for Landing Pages (BE + FE)
TC01 – Verify landing pages are created correctly in Sanity Studio

Steps:

Open Sanity Studio.

Navigate to the section where new landing pages are defined.

Create a new landing page using the provided schema (Hero Content, Content, Tags, SEO, Data Layer).

Save the page.
Expected Result:

Landing page is created successfully with all required sections.

Page appears in the correct content folder (root content or Generic Content Pages as defined).

TC02 – Verify FE retrieves landing page data from Studio

Steps:

In FE, navigate to the new landing page route.

Verify that the FE query pulls data from Sanity correctly.
Expected Result:

Data from Sanity (Hero, SEO, Content sections) is displayed correctly.

No missing fields or broken components.

TC03 – Verify FE lists all landing pages

Steps:

Navigate to the route that lists all landing pages (Next.js structure).

Observe the list generated by the query that retrieves all landing pages.
Expected Result:

All landing pages created in Sanity appear in the list.

No duplicates, missing pages, or ordering issues.

TC04 – Verify FE displays individual landing page details

Steps:

From the list, click on a landing page.

Verify that the hero, SEO, and content sections load correctly.
Expected Result:

Landing page renders all expected sections: Hero, SEO, Content.

Layout and structure match design requirements.

TC05 – Verify navigation structure for new landing pages (Next.js routes)

Steps:

Try accessing the newly created landing pages through the Next.js route structure.

Confirm route follows the expected URL format.
Expected Result:

Each landing page is accessible at the correct URL.

No 404 or routing errors.



QA Pass Comment

All test scenarios for the new landing pages have been executed. Landing pages are created successfully in Sanity with all required sections, FE routes render as expected, data is pulled correctly from Studio, and the list + detail pages display the hero, SEO, and content sections properly. No issues observed — functionality is working as expected.
